   138	def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
   139	    """
   140	    Launch four teal square beams across the board, bending at obstacles by shape.
   141	
   142	    Input structure:
   143	    - A single main grid only; this variant removes the legend band entirely.
   144	    - The grid contains one solid teal (8) square, a uniform background, and 3-4 colored obstacle rectangles.
   145	    - Each obstacle is deliberately non-square, so its geometry visibly encodes a turn direction.
   146	
   147	    Rule:
   148	    - Keep the full grid size; nothing is cropped away in the output.
   149	    - Emit four cardinal beams from the teal square, treating the beam as a sliding sz-by-sz copy of the square.
   150	    - As the beam advances, it paints teal onto background cells only.
   151	    - If the next beam footprint would hit an obstacle, turn in place instead of entering it:
   152	    - wide obstacle (width > height) => clockwise turn; tall obstacle (height > width) => counterclockwise turn.
   153	    - Continue until the beam would leave the grid.
   154	
   155	    Key insight: The removed legend is replaced by the obstacle rectangles themselves; their aspect ratio is the
   156	    only signal that determines whether a beam bends clockwise or counterclockwise.
   157	    """
